WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.560 --> 00:00:05.120
The Book of Boba Fett Fett has finally&nbsp;
come to a close, as the famous bounty&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:05.120 --> 00:00:10.720
hunter rallies his forces for battle against&nbsp;
the Pyke Syndicate and its enforcer, Cad Bane.

00:00:10.720 --> 00:00:15.920
The series goes in some interesting directions in&nbsp;
Chapter 5 and Chapter 6, which heavily focus on&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:15.920 --> 00:00:21.680
the Mandalorian Din Djarin, the Yoda lookalike&nbsp;
Grogu, and the legendary Luke Skywalker.

00:00:21.680 --> 00:00:27.920
But the finale brings everything back to Tatooine&nbsp;
as Boba's battle with the Pykes escalates into an&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:27.920 --> 00:00:34.960
all-out war across Mos Espa. Does the finale have&nbsp;
ramifications for the wider Star Wars universe?&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:34.960 --> 00:00:40.960
More importantly, does it tease what's coming up&nbsp;
ahead in The Mandalorian Season 3? Well, sort of.

00:00:42.000 --> 00:00:42.500
"For now?"

00:00:43.520 --> 00:00:44.480
"We wait."

00:00:44.480 --> 00:00:50.800
The tension on Tatooine cranks up from the very&nbsp;
beginning of the final season 1 episode, as Boba,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:50.800 --> 00:00:57.200
Fennec Shand, and the Mandalorian survey the&nbsp;
Sanctuary wreckage — R.I.P. Garsa Fwip. Boba also&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:57.200 --> 00:01:02.720
faces an emotional blow as Bane reveals that the&nbsp;
Pykes are actually the ones who killed the Tusken&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:02.720 --> 00:01:08.560
tribe, not the Nikto Sand Riders. The massacre&nbsp;
is revenge for their attack on the Spice train.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:08.560 --> 00:01:14.400
All of this only hardens Boba's determination to&nbsp;
rid Tatooine of the Syndicate once and for all.

00:01:14.400 --> 00:01:18.240
But when the battle for Mos Espa&nbsp;
gets started, writer Jon Favreau&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:18.240 --> 00:01:22.800
and director Robert Rodriguez deliver a&nbsp;
pulse-pounding fight for the very soul&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:22.800 --> 00:01:28.080
of Tatooine. Luckily, Boba, Din, and&nbsp;
Fennec aren't alone in their struggle.

00:01:28.080 --> 00:01:34.000
The big cliffhanger at the end of Chapter 6&nbsp;
sees Luke Skywalker offer Grogu a choice — he&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:34.000 --> 00:01:40.080
can either take the Beskar chainmail and return to&nbsp;
Din Djarin, or he can pick Yoda's old lightsaber&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:40.080 --> 00:01:45.120
and train to become a fully-fledged Jedi. On one&nbsp;
hand, it would be great to see him train in the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:45.120 --> 00:01:50.400
Force and master his abilities, but we all know&nbsp;
that he really belongs with his surrogate father.

00:01:50.400 --> 00:01:56.320
Thankfully, Favreau gives fans what they want as&nbsp;
R2-D2 lands Luke's X-wing in Peli Motto's hangar,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:56.320 --> 00:02:00.960
with Grogu sitting comfortably in the pilot's&nbsp;
seat. Because Grogu's memory is clouded,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:00.960 --> 00:02:06.960
he doesn't have many meaningful connections — and&nbsp;
although Luke and Ahsoka Tano are kind to him,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:06.960 --> 00:02:09.440
he's got a much closer bond with Din.

00:02:09.440 --> 00:02:14.240
At least his brief time with Luke means he already&nbsp;
has a better grip on his Force abilities than he&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:14.240 --> 00:02:20.000
did before, which is quite useful when the streets&nbsp;
of Mos Espa erupt into a deadly firefight when the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:20.000 --> 00:02:25.520
other gangs of the city betray their treaty with&nbsp;
Boba, attacking Boba's enforcers. It's not exactly&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:25.520 --> 00:02:30.400
surprising, since the different factions are&nbsp;
clearly just out for money rather than respect.

00:02:30.400 --> 00:02:34.800
Although, things start to look dire when&nbsp;
the hordes of Pykes deploy two deadly&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:34.800 --> 00:02:40.480
Scorpenek droids. Oh dear. Nevertheless,&nbsp;
Boba has some other backup to rely on.

00:02:41.120 --> 00:02:45.600
The devastating power of the Scorpenek&nbsp;
droids causes chaos in the battle because&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:45.600 --> 00:02:49.280
their shields are too strong for Boba's&nbsp;
army to blast through with any of their&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:49.280 --> 00:02:54.320
weapons. Din Djarin even whips out the Darksaber&nbsp;
to try to penetrate the shields, but it has no&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:54.320 --> 00:02:58.960
effect at all — although he probably needs some&nbsp;
more training to carry its weight. But then,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:58.960 --> 00:03:04.960
the finale pays off on Chapter 3's promise as&nbsp;
Boba finally rides his Rancor into battle. The&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:04.960 --> 00:03:10.240
monster's power quickly overwhelms the first&nbsp;
Scorpenek droid, with a little help from Grogu.

00:03:10.240 --> 00:03:13.200
Luke's training comes in handy&nbsp;
for the little green Force-user,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:13.200 --> 00:03:17.040
as he yanks a key component from the&nbsp;
droid's parts that makes it vulnerable.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:17.040 --> 00:03:21.440
Grogu clearly has a fondness for shiny metal&nbsp;
objects, because it's pretty reminiscent&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:21.440 --> 00:03:25.600
of the way he grabs that ball from the&nbsp;
Razor Crest in The Mandalorian Season 1.

00:03:25.600 --> 00:03:31.280
After the Rancor finishes the first droid off,&nbsp;
Boba steers it to the second, quickly eviscerating&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:31.280 --> 00:03:35.760
it. The destruction of the droids and the sheer&nbsp;
power of the Rancor sends the Pykes running,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:35.760 --> 00:03:41.040
which is a nice piece of symbolism: Tatooine&nbsp;
is taking itself back from its oppressors.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:41.040 --> 00:03:46.800
Although, it's not over just yet, as Cad Bane&nbsp;
shows his face again to try to kill Boba.

00:03:46.800 --> 00:03:52.320
Cad Bane's arrival at the end of Chapter 6 calls&nbsp;
back to the Western genre which George Lucas was&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:52.320 --> 00:03:58.160
originally inspired by when creating Star Wars&nbsp;
back in the 70s. Director Robert Rodriguez leans&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:58.160 --> 00:04:03.520
into the gunslinging genre once again for Boba&nbsp;
Fett's duel with Bane in the finale, as they trade&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:03.520 --> 00:04:08.800
insults in a tense standoff. Bane even points&nbsp;
out that they've known each other a long time,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:08.800 --> 00:04:13.040
calling back to the times they crossed&nbsp;
paths during The Clone Wars animated series.

00:04:13.040 --> 00:04:17.120
Bane makes it clear that he might be an old&nbsp;
man, but he's still quicker than Boba when it&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:17.120 --> 00:04:21.760
comes to a quickdraw gunfight. For a minute,&nbsp;
it even looks like Bane might kill Boba.

00:04:21.760 --> 00:04:28.640
"Look out for yourself.&nbsp;
Everything else is weakness."

00:04:29.360 --> 00:04:34.800
But this is Boba Fett, so he doesn't go down&nbsp;
that easily. Instead, he uses his gaffi stick&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:34.800 --> 00:04:40.080
to swiftly knock Bane to the ground — symbolizing&nbsp;
how his new strength comes from having a family.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:40.080 --> 00:04:45.040
He even avenges his fallen Tusken tribe&nbsp;
by killing Bane with the stick... Sure,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:45.040 --> 00:04:48.880
he's a fan-favorite villain, but his&nbsp;
death has been a long time coming.
 
 

00:04:49.440 --> 00:04:54.720
Cad Bane's death causes the few remaining Pykes&nbsp;
to retreat — let's face it, if he can't take Boba&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:54.720 --> 00:05:00.080
Fett down, who can? So, it looks like this is a&nbsp;
new era for Tatooine now that the crime lord has&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:00.080 --> 00:05:04.880
liberated the planet from the Pyke Syndicate.&nbsp;
Fennec Shand even wipes out that gang's last&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:04.880 --> 00:05:10.080
foothold on the planet by killing their leader and&nbsp;
executing Mayor Mok Shaiz [MOCK SHAYZ]. Leaving&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:10.080 --> 00:05:14.720
either of them alive would mean that the&nbsp;
Spice trade on Tatooine could start up again.

00:05:14.720 --> 00:05:20.320
Some time after the big battle, Fett reacts&nbsp;
uncomfortably to the Mos Espa residents bowing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:20.320 --> 00:05:24.640
and calling him "Lord Boba." He remarks to&nbsp;
Fennec that they're not cut out to rule– a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:24.640 --> 00:05:28.720
surprising comment considering everything&nbsp;
they’ve gone through to get here. However,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:28.720 --> 00:05:34.080
this is a new role for Fett: murderous Bounty&nbsp;
Hunter turned Local Hero. Fennec responds,

00:05:34.640 --> 00:05:38.240
“If not us, then who?”

00:05:38.240 --> 00:05:43.120
The finale ends with Din flying his Naboo&nbsp;
Starfighter through space as Grogu sits in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:43.120 --> 00:05:47.600
the pod behind him. The little green Force-user&nbsp;
even pesters him to fly at high speeds,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:47.600 --> 00:05:53.040
and Din — like any parent — reluctantly obliges.&nbsp;
It's not clear where they're headed, although it's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:53.040 --> 00:05:57.920
possible Din wants to redeem himself in the waters&nbsp;
of Mandalore underneath the planet's mines.
 
 

00:05:58.480 --> 00:06:03.040
Of course, it wouldn't be a Disney+ series&nbsp;
if there wasn't a post-credits scene teasing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:03.040 --> 00:06:07.600
the future of the galaxy! The brief scene&nbsp;
takes audiences back to Boba's quarters,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:07.600 --> 00:06:11.680
where Cobb Vanth is recuperating&nbsp;
in the gunslinger's bacta tank,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:11.680 --> 00:06:15.120
where The Modifier from Chapter 4 is&nbsp;
keeping an eye on him. This clearly&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:15.120 --> 00:06:20.720
suggests that Vanth is severely wounded&nbsp;
when shot by Cad Bane, but not killed.

00:06:20.720 --> 00:06:24.640
It'll be interesting to see how the&nbsp;
modification artist fixes his injuries,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:24.640 --> 00:06:27.920
although he's definitely going to need some&nbsp;
new armor to wear instead of just a shirt&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:27.920 --> 00:06:32.880
and a bandana. Maybe Din Djarin can give him&nbsp;
some spare Beskar in The Mandalorian Season 3.

